WEBVTT

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:13.700
This is really neat!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.520
When do we eat?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.280
First, we have to catch some fish.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:26.520
In order to catch fish, you have to do this.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.720
Here we go.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:30.400
That's it.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.500
Then drop it into the water.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.600
How do you know so much about fishing?

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.510
Grandpa taught me.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.060
We spent a lot of time fishing together.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:58.740
Now, the important thing is to get the hook close to the fish.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:00:59.800
All right?

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:00.680
Like this.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:11.320
I think I see some fish right under us, Dad.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.340
Oh, not a chance!

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.880
I just saw a big one!

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:16.860
Hi, there!

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:18.920
What's your name?

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:19.480
Albert.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.120
Are you all alone?

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.000
Yes, sir.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.280
How old are you, Albert?

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:25.280
I'm ten.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:28.920
Where's your father?

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.040
He's up there at the lodge.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.740
Yes, sir.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:42.060
The water's pretty deep here.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:43.610
I'll watch him, Dad.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.340
What time is it?

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.180
It's almost lunchtime, and no fish yet.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.220
I can go up to the lodge for some hot dogs and drinks.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.420
No way!

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.640
We're here to catch our lunch.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:07.960
That's right.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:08.420
I forgot!

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.580
The right magic.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:12.800
You remember?

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:18.300
Well, first, you have to turn your hat around like this.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.260
Then you close your eyes and say the magic words.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.980
Fish, fish, send me a fish.

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:39.720
Fish, fish, send me a fish.... I got one!

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:40.880
See, it works!

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.900
It's a big one!

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.460
Well, it always worked for me, too.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.180
Grandpa, get the net, please!

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.240
Dad, you got one, too!

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.400
You bet I have!

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:00.240
Easy, Philip, easy.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.280
Sorry, Dad.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.480
Yes, but you did, and we've got our lunch.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.180
Let's build a fire and cook it!

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.900
Come on, Albert, you can help us!

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:24.820
I want to stay here and fish.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.620
All right, but be careful.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:39.620
Is it finished yet?

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:40.700
I think so.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.300
I hope you like your fish well done.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.100
Burned, you mean.

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:49.000
Hey, I'm a doctor, not a chef.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.160
Help! Help! I can't swim!

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.350
Dad! Grandpa! He fell in!

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.040
Robbie, run to the car!

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.390
Breathe, Albert!
